<edge source="iran_economic_and_hormuz::sanctions_strength" target="treasury_bond_market_tug::bond_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger sanctions increase compliance risk for banks and trading counterparties (fear of secondary sanctions), inducing deleveraging and reduced willingness to provide repo or dealer intermediation and thereby narrowing market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_economic_and_hormuz</data>
  <data key="d39">treasury_bond_market_tug</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_economic_and_hormuz::sanctions_strength" target="us_canada_trade_spat::corporate_investment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter, broader sanctions raise compliance costs and banking/payment frictions for firms operating across the US‑Canada corridor, increasing legal/regulatory uncertainty that leads companies to delay or reduce cross‑border investment commitments.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_economic_and_hormuz</data>
  <data key="d39">us_canada_trade_spat</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_economic_and_hormuz::sanctions_strength" target="us_china_tech_competitio::regulatory_enforcement" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">An intensification of sanctions expands legal authorities and political will to close loopholes and to target dual‑use channels, triggering more frequent and stricter export controls, investigations and interdiction actions against AI‑relevant goods and services.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_economic_and_hormuz</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_competitio</data>
</edge>
