<edge source="us_canada_trade_spat::supply_chain_disruption" target="russia_ukraine_war::logistics_ammo_stocks" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Cross‑border delays, customs slowdowns and rerouting caused by the US–Canada trade spat interrupt just‑in‑time shipments of ammunition components and propellants that feed North American production lines, directly lowering on‑hand munitions and spare‑parts stocks available for Ukraine support.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_canada_trade_spat</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_canada_trade_spat::supply_chain_disruption" target="treasury_bond_market_tug::bond_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Material cross‑border supply shocks amplify price volatility and hedging flows, leading dealers to reduce inventory and widen bid/ask spreads, which directly reduces Treasury market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_canada_trade_spat</data>
  <data key="d39">treasury_bond_market_tug</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_canada_trade_spat::supply_chain_disruption" target="us_china_tech_competitio::capital_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Repeated cross‑border delays and higher transaction costs increase project execution risk and expected returns for AI infrastructure, prompting financiers and corporates to delay or withdraw planned capital allocations into the contested ecosystem.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_canada_trade_spat</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_competitio</data>
</edge>
