<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_strike_rate" target="treasury_bond_market_tug::bond_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">High-tempo strikes that damage physical infrastructure and raise counterparty/settlement risk cause dealers to pull inventories and widen bid-ask spreads, reducing bond market depth and tradability.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">treasury_bond_market_tug</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_strike_rate" target="us_canada_trade_spat::supply_chain_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">A surge in strikes against ports, rail hubs and shipping in the Black Sea and surrounding regions forces rerouting and longer transit times for container and bulk shipments, cascading into delays and higher transaction costs for North American firms that depend on tightly timed international inputs and thereby increasing US‑Canada cross‑border supply frictions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_canada_trade_spat</data>
</edge>
