  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A fall in producible AI hardware capacity (e.g., curtailed chip output) directly produces component shortages that force rerouting, delays and higher transaction costs across North American supply chains, increasing US–Canada supply disruptions (conversely, capacity growth reduces disruption).</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_competitio</data>
